+// meaningful slice of it, because splitting a small buffer costs more than the
+// concurrency it buys:
+//
+//   - Series are spread over the shards by hash, so a shard can fill up while
+//     others still have room. The capacity lost to that imbalance is
+//     proportional to 1/sqrt(capacity): about 10% at a capacity of 100, but
+//     only ~0.5% at 100000 and ~0.1% at 1000000.
+//   - Eviction becomes per shard, so which series survives a full buffer (or a
+//     shrink) is decided within a shard rather than across the whole storage.
+//     That reordering is invisible at scale but very visible in a handful of
+//     slots.
